"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n<section class=\"section service-editorial\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><nav class=\"service-jump-links\" aria-label=\"On this service page\"><a href=\"#service-work\">Services</a><a href=\"#service-method\">Repair &amp; installation</a><a href=\"#service-quote\">Costs &amp; quote</a><a href=\"#service-faq\">FAQs</a><a href=\"#service-booking\">Book a visit</a></nav><aside class=\"service-answer\" data-service-answer><h2>What to do next</h2><p>For an active leak from a damaged pipe, tell us the location, current flow and whether the pipe is exposed. Do not enter water near electrical equipment or approach unstable surfaces to investigate. We assess the affected section and accessible connections, then quote the repair and any access work. If the source is uncertain, leak investigation may be needed first. Wall, floor and other building restoration are not automatically included in the plumbing repair.</p><p><a href=\"insights-reporting-a-plumbing-leak.html\">What to record before a leak assessment</a>. <a href=\"contact.html?service=burst-pipe-repair-perth.html\">Request an assessment and written quote</a>.</p></aside><div id=\"service-work\" class=\"service-editorial-part\"><h2>Repairing damaged water pipes and leaking connections</h2><h3>An exposed pipe or accessible joint</h3><p>When the damaged pipe or joint is visible, the repair still depends on the pipe material, condition and accessible connections. We assess the affected section rather than assuming a patch or replacement fitting will suit every installation. Let us know where the water is escaping and whether the flow is ongoing.</p>\n<h3>A leak behind a wall or below ground</h3><p>Concealed damage needs the source and access requirements established before corrective work is agreed. We explain the proposed opening or excavation scope and how it relates to the plumbing repair. If the source is not yet clear, our <a href=\"water-leak-detection-perth.html\">water leak detection service</a> provides the related investigation pathway.</p>\n<h3>Property damage and managed-property coordination</h3><p>The plumbing repair and the repair of wet finishes or contents are separate matters. For rental or managed properties, send the approval contact and work-order reference with the location of the affected pipe. This helps us coordinate access without assuming that building repairs or insurance decisions fall within the plumbing scope.</p><figure class=\"service-editorial-figure\"><img loading=\"lazy\"\n            class=\"service-editorial-image\"\n            src=\"plumbing-leak-perth.png\"\n            width=\"1672\"\n            height=\"941\"\n            alt=\"Plumbing repair work in an Australian laundry\" srcset=\"plumbing-leak-perth-480.webp 480w, plumbing-leak-perth-800.webp 800w, plumbing-leak-perth-1200.webp 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1000px) 50vw, 380px\"></figure></div>\n<div id=\"service-method\" class=\"service-editorial-part\"><h2>Our burst-pipe assessment and repair approach</h2><p>At the property, we establish the affected section, its connections and the access available for repair. The assessment determines whether the agreed work involves a joint, a fitting or replacement of a section of pipe. We explain the proposed materials and any work needed to reach the damaged area before the repair is authorised.</p>\n<h3>A defined repair scope before additional work</h3><p>A short exposed repair is different from tracing and reaching a concealed pipe. The written quote separates the agreed plumbing work from extra access, additional pipe replacement and reinstatement. If more extensive deterioration becomes apparent, we explain the finding and any change to the scope rather than proceeding with an unexplained extension of the job.</p>\n<p>After completing the authorised work, we check the repaired section and discuss what was done and any further issue observed. We explain any recommended follow-up and confirm the agreed job with you. For other water-supply faults or fixture work, explore our <a href=\"plumbing.html\">Perth plumbing services</a> and include the additional requirement when requesting a visit.</p></div><p class=\"service-trade-note\">Our Perth plumbing and electrical work is carried out by appropriately licensed trades. Licence details are available on request.</p><p class=\"service-safety\"><strong>Safety:</strong> Avoid water near electrical equipment, unstable surfaces and any hazardous area. Do not put yourself at risk to investigate the damaged pipe. For immediate danger, Call 000.</p><!-- keyword-gap:start --><div class=\"keyword-gap-content\" data-keyword-gap><div class=\"keyword-gap-part\" id=\"learn-about-burst-pipe-repair-perth\"><h2>Burst pipe repairs Perth: symptoms and service choices</h2><h3>Signs of a leaking pipe inside a wall</h3><p>Dampness, staining or unexpected water can justify investigation, but similar signs can come from other sources. Report the location and timing without opening walls; water near electrical equipment requires safety-first action.</p><ul class=\"intent-links\"><li><a href=\"insights-reporting-a-plumbing-leak.html\">Reporting water location and timing safely</a></li></ul></div></div><!-- keyword-gap:end --></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
},
