"html": "\n<section class=\"section service-quote\" id=\"service-quote\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><h2>Burst-pipe repair costs and access requirements</h2><div class=\"price-guide\" aria-labelledby=\"ellis-price-guide\">\n            <div class=\"shell\">\n              <div class=\"price-guide__intro\">\n                <p class=\"price-guide__kicker\">Ellis Price Guide</p>\n                <h2 id=\"ellis-price-guide\">Burst-pipe repair price guide</h2>\n                <p>\n                  A practical guide for a standard burst-pipe repair at a Perth\n                  property.\n                </p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"price-guide__grid\">\n                <article class=\"price-guide__item\">\n                  <h3>Burst-pipe repair</h3>\n                  <p class=\"price-guide__range\">AUD $275–$990</p>\n                  <p class=\"price-guide__unit\">per repair · incl. GST</p>\n                </article>\n              </div>\n              <p class=\"price-guide__notice\">\n                <strong>Guide conditions:</strong> These AUD ranges are for\n                standard-hours, standard-scope work and are incl. GST. Access,\n                materials, extra pipe, cable or circuit work, compliance work,\n                emergency or after-hours work and unforeseen repairs are\n                confirmed in a written quote before work proceeds.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n          </div><h3>What your written quote covers</h3><p>The damaged section, pipe material, location and access affect the repair plan. An exposed connection is a different scope from a pipe behind a wall or below ground. The assessment establishes which section requires repair, what access is needed and what additional work is included before the written quote is agreed.</p><p>The final written quote sets out the work included, materials and any agreed additional tasks. We explain changes to the scope before extra work proceeds. <a href=\"contact.html?service=burst-pipe-repair-perth.html\">Request a burst-pipe repair quote</a>.</p></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"id": "service-faq",
"kind": "faq",
"container": "\n<section class=\"section faq service-editorial-faq\" id=\"service-faq\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><h2>Burst Pipe Repairs Perth FAQs</h2><!-- site-intent:start --><div class=\"intent-content\" data-site-intent><h3>An active pipe leak and an uncertain source need different scopes</h3><p>An exposed damaged connection may allow a defined repair. Water appearing through a ceiling or wall may first need source investigation and access planning. Explain the current flow and any affected electrical area from a safe location; do not remove building finishes to prepare for the visit.</p><ul class=\"intent-links\"><li><a href=\"water-leak-detection-perth.html\">Investigating an uncertain water source</a></li><li><a href=\"plumbing.html\">Related plumbing repairs and quote conditions</a></li><li><a href=\"shower-plumbing-repairs-perth.html\">Shower Plumbing Leak Repairs Perth</a></li><li><a href=\"emergency-plumber-perth.html\">24-Hour Emergency Plumber Perth</a></li></ul><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:0:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:0:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:1:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:1:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:2:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:2:answer}}</details></div><!-- site-intent:end --><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:3:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:3:answer}}</details>\n<details><summary>{{ppp:faq:4:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:4:answer}}</details>\n<details><summary>{{ppp:faq:5:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:5:answer}}</details>\n<details><summary>{{ppp:faq:6:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:6:answer}}</details>\n<details><summary>{{ppp:faq:7:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:7:answer}}</details>\n<details><summary>{{ppp:faq:8:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:8:answer}}</details>\n<details><summary>{{ppp:faq:9:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:9:answer}}</details></div></section>" as TrustedHtml,
"items": [
{
"question": "Will the pipe-repair quote include wall or ceiling restoration?",
"answer": "<p>Only when the written scope expressly includes it. Confirm pipe access, repair, testing and any separate restoration or other trade work rather than assuming that repairing the pipe restores every affected surface.</p>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"question": "Does an active leak guarantee an immediate call-out?",
"answer": "<p>No. Call to explain the current condition and confirm availability and charges. Keep people clear of hazards; a normal booking request is not a substitute for emergency or utility action where needed.</p>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"question": "What are the signs of a burst or leaking pipe inside a wall?",
"answer": "<p>Unexplained damp patches, stains or water may indicate a concealed leak, but inspection must distinguish plumbing from other sources. <a href=\"#learn-about-burst-pipe-repair-perth\">Read the explanation.</a></p>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"question": "Do I need to diagnose the problem first?",
"answer": "<p>No. Describe the observable change and property context. We inspect the affected area on site to establish the cause and confirm the repair scope. If more access is needed, we agree it with you first.</p>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"question": "Can I send photos?",
"answer": "<p>Photos are optional: email safely taken photos to maxinemaintenance.au@outlook.com. You can contact us without photos. Do not approach a hazard, remove covers or dismantle equipment to take a photo.</p>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"question": "What should I do first if a pipe bursts?",
"answer": "<p>Put people and electrical safety first. If it is safe and familiar, isolate the water supply; otherwise keep clear and contact us with the details.</p>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"question": "When should I use the water leak page instead?",
"answer": "<p>Use Water Leak Detection for an unexplained leak or damp area where there is no visible failed pipe. Use this page when water is actively escaping or a pipe or fitting has visibly failed.</p>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"question": "Do I need to know the pipe type?",
"answer": "<p>No. A description of the location, water flow and affected area is more useful than a guess about the cause.</p>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"question": "Can a property manager make the booking?",
"answer": "<p>Yes. Include access, occupant and work-order details in the enquiry.</p>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"question": "Will the quote include repairing the wall or floor?",
"answer": "<p>The written scope states what access and reinstatement work is included. Plumbing repairs do not automatically include replacement finishes or separate building work. We clarify those items before proceeding.</p>" as TrustedHtml
}
]
},
{
"id": "service-booking",
"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n<section class=\"section contact-band service-booking\" id=\"service-booking\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><h2>Book burst-pipe repair in Perth</h2><p>Tell us the suburb, location of the pipe, whether water is actively escaping and any access restrictions. If it is safe, describe whether the damaged section is exposed; do not approach a hazard to find out. Our local team covers <a href=\"service-areas.html\">all six Perth service regions</a> from our office at 140 St Georges Terrace, Perth WA 6000.</p><p>Call to discuss the work or send the property details through our enquiry form. You do not need to diagnose the fault or complete a technical inspection before contacting us.</p><a class=\"button\" href=\"tel:0413477667\">Call 0413 477 667</a> <a class=\"button service-book-button\" href=\"contact.html?service=burst-pipe-repair-perth.html\">Request a visit &amp; written quote</a></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
